{"id": "EUVD-2026-82236", "enisaUuid": "b7b7e691-b1ca-3bb3-a0e1-5a4a4119012a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: lg-laptop: Fix LED resource handling\n\nThe event notification callback might access kbd_backlight even\nwhen it was not successfully registered with the LED subsystem.\nThe same happens inside acpi_remove(), where the LED devices are\nunregistered unconditionally.\n\nFix this by tracking the availability of the kbd_backlight LED\ndevice and use devm_led_classdev_register() to let devres take\ncare of unregistering the LED devices during removal. For this\nthe parent device of the LED devices is changed to the native\nplatform device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc45f6e4b86c2fa1cf742c23a373d777d066aa25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fbfe3714f645b6c64c9ba8faa83b27e4c9f2edd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a85e2d35e54248aca39bad4f4152ed34de1995f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/acc190322250562d5f28860f4ae1ebaf3e304fc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e91964aa74ab261aa15d9d96318eded2fd9d22a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93128", "GHSA-9hr7-r765-xm77"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b9949d8-4b36-387b-ade9-2c4df2373034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae26278829a80ad0e60ff004de71e9276cee5dc0 <9a85e2d35e54248aca39bad4f4152ed34de1995f"}, {"id": "2c56ab6a-610e-3aba-ac21-ca63452c8737", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae26278829a80ad0e60ff004de71e9276cee5dc0 <fc45f6e4b86c2fa1cf742c23a373d777d066aa25"}, {"id": "34129934-313f-3d1b-a6e1-274022b92fc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3e56bb1b-6e3f-395b-8844-3a67b1e5fc49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae26278829a80ad0e60ff004de71e9276cee5dc0 <acc190322250562d5f28860f4ae1ebaf3e304fc2"}, {"id": "6ea9d1e5-2f9b-3fb4-83ab-2289035aa614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "bf951368-1bb9-3a11-a04c-ce30431adf46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "c0ed82da-14a5-38ce-addd-7e730117f789", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "d238bbe3-6a86-36a2-8132-7ed1872630ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae26278829a80ad0e60ff004de71e9276cee5dc0 <3e91964aa74ab261aa15d9d96318eded2fd9d22a"}, {"id": "da57d722-aae2-3d00-b742-d29ee8978c05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae26278829a80ad0e60ff004de71e9276cee5dc0 <4fbfe3714f645b6c64c9ba8faa83b27e4c9f2edd"}, {"id": "e6d3095d-f4fc-34ea-b350-da42bfd98e95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f1149a15-9d0d-30dc-96cb-ffd449aaeb78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "fe40e7ff-482e-37bb-a4c7-c6ff5339fb15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "23bd7af5-83ae-39d6-949a-8eeed7e53258", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}